gbcli's per-pixel layer-identity patch for SameBoy ea667ad.

Observation only: display.c writes one tag per drawn pixel (GBCLI_LAYER_*,
named in display.h: background, window, or GBCLI_LAYER_OBJECT + the OAM index)
into an optional side buffer, and reads that new pointer only to test it.
display.h carries the tag on the BG and OAM FIFO items; gb.h holds the buffer
pointer. With no buffer attached, the work left is a predictable branch per
pixel, the two extra FIFO-item bytes and their stores, and the OAM index kept
in render_line's object buffer (see the vendoring doc for the measured cost).

Applied by scripts/vendor-sameboy.sh after re-vendoring. The vendored tree in
this repository already has it applied, so a normal build needs no patch step.
Rebase it (do not drop it) if SameBoy's commit moves.
